    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0155" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg85"/>

                <head>Mr. Hale to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 89.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Agency and Consulate General U. S. of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Alexandria,
                            Egypt,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir :</hi> A telegram from Paris, on the afternoon of
                    the 8th, brought the intelligence of the attempted assassination in that capital
                    of the Emperor, Alexander <pb facs="0156" n="86" xml:id="pg86"/> II, of Russia.
                    The tidings were communicated by the Russian consul general, in a circular to
                    his colleagues, announcing that a Te Deum would be sung at the church of the
                    national faith here the next morning, in celebration of the miraculous escape of
                    the Emperor. I made a reply in writing to this circular, and attended the
                    solemnity of the Te Deum together with my vice-consul and first dragoman.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES HALE.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
